# Spring Boot Revision Notes

## 1. Project Structure — Entity Folder

In Spring Boot, entities are stored in either:
- `model` — more common in older conventions, groups all domain objects
- `entity` — more explicit, signals JPA/database-mapped classes

```
com.example.myapp/
├── controller/
├── service/
├── repository/
├── model/        ← option 1
└── entity/       ← option 2
```

Use `entity` if you also have DTOs or other model classes. Use `model` if entities are your only domain objects.

