## 2. OpenAPI Generator — Inline Objects

### Problem
When a response schema is defined **inline** (anonymously), the generator auto-names it `InlineObject1`, `InlineObject2`, etc.

```yaml
# ❌ This generates InlineObject1
SingleCommentResponse:
  content:
    application/json:
      schema:
        type: object        # anonymous inline object
        properties:
          comment:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Comment'
```

### Fix 1 — Extract to `components/schemas`
```yaml
components:
  schemas:
    SingleCommentBody:
      type: object
      properties:
        comment:
          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Comment'
```
Then reference it:
```yaml
SingleCommentResponse:
  content:
    application/json:
      schema:
        $ref: '#/components/schemas/SingleCommentBody'
```

### Fix 2 — Add a `title` field (simpler)
```yaml
SingleCommentResponse:
  content:
    application/json:
      schema:
        title: SingleCommentResponse   # ← generator uses this as the class name
        type: object
        properties:
          comment:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Comment'
```

**Rule:** Any inline `type: object` in a response/request body triggers auto-naming. Use `title` or extract to `components/schemas` to control the name.

