## 4. Java Records

A **record** is a special class (Java 16+) designed as a **pure immutable data carrier**.

```java
public record User(String username, String email) {}
```

Automatically generates:
- Constructor with all fields
- Getters (named `username()` not `getUsername()`)
- `toString()`
- `equals()`
- `hashCode()`

### Custom constructor for validation
```java
public record User(String username, String email) {

    public User {
        if (username == null || username.isBlank()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Username cannot be blank");
        }
    }

    public String displayName() {
        return username.toUpperCase();
    }
}
```

### Records vs Lombok
| | Records | Lombok |
|---|---|---|
| Immutable | ✅ Always | ❌ Optional |
| Setters | ❌ Not supported | ✅ Supported |
| JPA Entities | ❌ Not suitable | ✅ Suitable |
| DTOs / Response objects | ✅ Great fit | ✅ Also works |

Records are best for **immutable DTOs and response objects**. Lombok is better for **JPA entities** since they need setters and a no-args constructor.

