## 5. `@Entity` and `@Table` Annotations

### `@Entity`
Tells JPA/Hibernate that this class is **mapped to a database table**. Required for JPA to manage the class.

```java
@Entity
public class User {
    @Id
    private Long id;
    private String username;
    private String email;
}
```

By default maps to a table with the same name as the class (`User` → `user`).

### `@Table`
Optional. Lets you **customize the table mapping**.

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "users")  // maps to "users" table instead of "user"
public class User {
    @Id
    private Long id;
    private String username;
    private String email;
}
```

Full options:
```java
@Table(
    name = "users",
    schema = "myschema",
    uniqueConstraints = {
        @UniqueConstraint(columnNames = {"username", "email"})
    },
    indexes = {
        @Index(columnList = "username")
    }
)
```

### Summary
| Annotation | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `@Entity` | ✅ Yes | Marks class as a JPA entity |
| `@Table` | ❌ No | Customizes table name, schema, constraints, indexes |

