## 6. Test Dependencies

### `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`
Provides testing support for the **web/MVC layer**. Bundles:
- `MockMvc` — simulate HTTP requests without starting a real server
- `@WebMvcTest` — loads only the web layer (controllers, filters, converters)
- JUnit 5, Mockito, AssertJ, Hamcrest, JsonPath

```java
@WebMvcTest(ArticlesController.class)
class ArticlesControllerTest {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @MockBean
    private ArticlesService articlesService;

    @Test
    void shouldReturnArticle() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/articles/my-slug"))
               .andExpect(status().isOk())
               .andExpect(jsonPath("$.article.slug").value("my-slug"));
    }
}
```

### DataSource in Tests
If your test loads the full Spring context (`@SpringBootTest`) but has no database configured, it will fail with:
```
Failed to determine a suitable driver class
```

Fix by adding H2 as an in-memory test database:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.h2database</groupId>
    <artifactId>h2</artifactId>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>
```

Or configure test properties:
```java
@SpringBootTest
@TestPropertySource(properties = {
    "spring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:mem:testdb",
    "spring.datasource.driver-class-name=org.h2.Driver",
    "spring.jpa.database-platform=org.hibernate.dialect.H2Dialect"
})
class ConduitApplicationTests {
    @Test
    void contextLoads() {}
}
```
